+  - Done: `slugify` now throws `TypeError` for non-object/null `options` ("options ...") and for a `maxLength` that is not an integer >= 1 ("options.maxLength ..."); AC1, AC6, AC7 tests pass.
+- [x] T2: Truncate at a word boundary, with the first-word hard cut (AC2–AC5) — done when: all tests pass with `node --test`.
+  - Done: after building the full slug, return it if it fits; else cut at index `maxLength` if a separator sits there, else before the last `-` in the first `maxLength` chars, else hard-cut the first word. Uses `lastIndexOf` with a start index instead of the design's `slice(0, maxLength + 1)` (same cut points, no extra string). All 26 tests pass with `node --test`.
+- [x] T3: Document the option in `slugify`'s JSDoc — done when: the JSDoc names `options.maxLength`, its valid values, the first-word rule, and the `TypeError`s.
+  - Done: JSDoc now describes `options.maxLength` (integer >= 1, `undefined` = no limit), word-boundary truncation, the first-word hard-cut rule, and both `TypeError`s. No other doc was made stale (architecture.md already points to the JSDoc; no README).
